foundation.question_text:
In the diagram $\overrightarrow{PQ}=\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\overrightarrow{QR}=\underset{\sim}{b}$.
Write $\overrightarrow{PR}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\underset{\sim}{b}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4.2,2.3);
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (Q) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[->,thick] (Q) -- (R) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{OA}=\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}=\underset{\sim}{b}$.
Write $\overrightarrow{AB}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\underset{\sim}{b}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.2,0.4);
\coordinate (B) at (1.0,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (A) node[midway,below right] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway,left] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the diagram to write $\overrightarrow{DE}+\overrightarrow{EF}$ as a single vector.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
