$OPRQ$ is a parallelogram with $\overrightarrow{OP}=\underset{\sim}{p}$ and $\overrightarrow{OQ}=\underset{\sim}{q}$.
Write $\overrightarrow{OR}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{p}$ and $\underset{\sim}{q}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4.2,2.2);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.2,2.2);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{p}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (Q) node[midway,left] {$\underset{\sim}{q}$};
\draw (P) -- (R);
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[below right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above left] at (Q) {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
