Write $\overrightarrow{WZ}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{u}$, $\underset{\sim}{v}$ and $\underset{\sim}{w}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (W) at (0,0);
\coordinate (X) at (2.8,-0.6);
\coordinate (Y) at (4.4,1.4);
\coordinate (Z) at (1.6,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (W) -- (X) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[->,thick] (X) -- (Y) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[->,thick] (Y) -- (Z) node[midway,above right] {$\underset{\sim}{w}$};
\node[left] at (W) {$W$};
\node[below] at (X) {$X$};
\node[right] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[above] at (Z) {$Z$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

