mastery.question_text:
$ABCD$ is a quadrilateral.
Write $\overrightarrow{AB}+\overrightarrow{BC}+\overrightarrow{CD}+\overrightarrow{DA}$ as a single vector.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.0,-0.4);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,1.8);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B);
\draw[->,thick] (B) -- (C);
\draw[->,thick] (C) -- (D);
\draw[->,thick] (D) -- (A);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{OA}=\underset{\sim}{a}$, $\overrightarrow{OB}=\underset{\sim}{b}$ and $\overrightarrow{OC}=\underset{\sim}{c}$.
Write $\overrightarrow{AB}+\overrightarrow{BC}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\underset{\sim}{c}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.0,0.6);
\coordinate (B) at (1.8,2.6);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.4,1.8);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (A) node[midway,below right] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (C) node[midway,below left] {$\underset{\sim}{c}$};
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
